{"metadata":{"title":"Running Code in the Godot Editor","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"There are cases where you might want some of your Swift code for your extension","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to run while it is being used in the Godot Editor.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Differences","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Variants","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Exports","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Signals","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RemoteProcedureCalls","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CustomTypes","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BindingNodes","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/MemoryManagement","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/TypesTranslation","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Documentation"],"anchor":"Articles-and-Tutorials","generated":true,"title":"Articles and Tutorials"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/runningineditor"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To achieve this, you can include the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".tool"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Godot"},{"type":"text","text":" macro,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"like this:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@Godot(.tool)","class Line3D: MeshInstance3D {","","    \/\/ This will be called in the editor","    override func _ready() {","\t\/\/ Run some code here","    }","","    \/\/ And so will this one","    override func _process(delta _: Double) {","\t\/\/ Check if we are running in the editor, or in the game","        if Engine.isEditorHint() {","            doEditorWork ()","        } else {","\t    doGameWork ()","\t}","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can use it for doing many things, but it is mostly useful in level design"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for visually presenting things that are hard to predict ourselves. Here are some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use cases:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you have a cannon that shoots cannonballs affected by physics (gravity),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you  can draw the cannonball’s trajectory in the editor, making level design a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lot easier."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you have jumppads with varying jump heights, you can draw the maximum jump"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"height a player would reach if it jumped on one, also making level design"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"easier."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If your player doesn’t use a sprite, but draws itself using code, you can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"make that drawing code execute in the editor to see your player.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":".tool","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" extensions run inside the editor, and let you access the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scene tree of the currently edited scene. This is a powerful feature which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also comes with caveats, as the editor does not include protections for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"potential misuse of "},{"code":"@Godot(.tool)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" scripts. Be extremely cautious when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"manipulating the scene tree, especially via "},{"code":"Node\/queueFree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as it can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cause crashes if you free a node while the editor runs logic involving it."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"warning","name":"Warning"},{"text":"Detecting the Editor","type":"heading","level":1,"anchor":"Detecting-the-Editor"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In your code, you can call the "},{"code":"Engine\/isEditorHint()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to determine whether"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the code is running inside the editor or in the game, and adjust your various"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"methods accordingly."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RunningInEditor","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Differences":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/differences","kind":"article","title":"SwiftGodot API differences to GDScript","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This document lists some common differences between GDSscript and SwiftGodot."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Differences"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/TypesTranslation":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/typestranslation","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Types Translation","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/TypesTranslation","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This document contains information on how type translation happens between Swift and Godot."}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/RemoteProcedureCalls":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RemoteProcedureCalls","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/remoteprocedurecalls","title":"Remote Procedure Calls","kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Rpc","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro to configure methods for Godot’s multiplayer RPC system.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Exports":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In Godot, class members can be exported. This means their value gets saved along"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the resource (such as the scene) they’re attached to. They will also be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"available for editing in the property editor. Exporting is done by using the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Export"},{"type":"text","text":" annotation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/exports","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Exports","type":"topic","title":"Exports","role":"article"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Documentation":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/documentation","kind":"article","title":"Documenting your Godot Extension","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If you are developing a Godot extension that is intended to be consumed from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Godot you might want to provide documentation for it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Documentation","role":"article"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/BindingNodes":{"role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BindingNodes","kind":"article","title":"Referencing Nodes from your Scene","abstract":[{"text":"You will find yourself referencing nodes from a scene in your code. In","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"GDScript, that is usually achieved by using the dollar sign and the name of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"object you want to reference.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/bindingnodes"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/MemoryManagement":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/memorymanagement","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/MemoryManagement","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftGodot surfaces various Godot types into the Swift universe in various ways:"}],"title":"Memory Management in SwiftGodot","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Variants":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/variants","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Variants","kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Variants","abstract":[{"text":"Follow up on the fundamental building block of Godot’s data types.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/CustomTypes":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CustomTypes","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/customtypes","title":"Using Custom Types","kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"You will typically extend the functionality of your Godot game by creating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"classes that derive from one of the various Godot types and adjust the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"behavior accordingly."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Signals":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Signals","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/signals","kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Signals","abstract":[{"text":"Signals in Godot are used by objects to post interesting events that are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"taking place, and can be used by users to easily add behavior and react","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to changes.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Framework to write Godot Game Extensions using the Swift Programming Language."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","title":"SwiftGodot","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"}}}